                <pb facs="1083" n="1071" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1071"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.01/10–445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Political Adviser
                        in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-11T20:00:00-05:00">October 11, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Concerning legal separation of Japan and Korea, referred to in your telegram
                    22, Oct 4, the Dept is giving the matter immediate consideration. You will be
                    informed of developments and if positive decision is reached the pertinent
                    directive will be telegraphed to GHQ.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
